      "id": "7hbClrgWjj1tfiJbZpId9",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 537.4170862833662,
      "y": -13173.00299835205,
      "width": 1221.1993408203125,
      "height": 2225,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b0a",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1560397033,
      "version": 790,
      "versionNonce": 1160105319,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1781073361311,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "class KVCacheManager:\n\n    self.coordinator = get_kv_cache_coordinator()\n    self.block_pool = self.coordinator.block_pool\n\n\nclass KVCacheCoordinator(ABC):\n\n    self.block_pool = BlockPool()\n\n\nclass BlockPool:\n\n    # Free block queue that constructs and manipulates a doubly linked\n    # list of free blocks (including eviction candidates when caching is\n    # enabled).\n    self.free_block_queue = FreeKVCacheBlockQueue(self.blocks)\n\n    # Cache for block lookup\n    self.cached_block_hash_to_block: BlockHashToBlockMap = BlockHashToBlockMap()\n\n\nclass FreeKVCacheBlockQueue:\n    \"\"\"This class organizes a list of KVCacheBlock objects to a doubly linked\n    list of free blocks. We implement this class instead of using Python\n    builtin deque to support removing a block in the middle of the queue\n    in O(1) time. To close the performance gap to the builtin deque which is\n    implemented in C++, this class does not allocate any Python objects when\n    manipulating the linked list. Instead, this class manipulates the\n    prev_free_block and next_free_block attributes of the given blocks.\n    该类将一组 `KVCacheBlock` 对象组织成一个空闲块双向链表。\n    我们选择实现该类而非使用 Python 内置的 `deque`，是为了支持在 O(1) 时间复杂度内移除队列中间的某个块。\n    为了缩小与 C++ 实现的内置 `deque` 之间的性能差距，该类在操作链表时不会分配任何 Python 对象，\n    而是直接操作给定块的 `prev_free_block` 和 `next_free_block` 属性。\n\n    The queue is ordered by block ID in the beginning. When a block is allocated\n    and then freed, it will be appended back with the eviction order:\n    1. The least recent used block is at the front (LRU).\n    2. If two blocks have the same last accessed time (allocated by the\n       same sequence), the one with more hash tokens (the tail of a block\n       chain) is at the front.\n    Note that we maintain this order by reversing the block order when free\n    blocks of a request. This operation is outside of this class.\n    初始状态下，队列按块 ID 排序。当一个块被分配并随后释放时，它会根据以下淘汰顺序重新加入队列：\n    1. 最近最少使用（LRU）的块位于队首。\n    2. 如果两个块的最后访问时间相同（即由同一序列分配），则包含更多哈希标记（hash tokens，即块链的末端）的块位于队首。\n    请注意，我们是通过在释放请求相关的空闲块时反转块的顺序来维护这一排序的；该操作在类外部进行。\n\n    Args:\n        blocks: A list of KVCacheBlock objects.\n    \"\"\"\n\n\nclass BlockHashToBlockMap:\n    \"\"\"\n    Cache of blocks that are used for prefix caching. It caches blocks\n    from hash directly to a block or multiple blocks\n    (i.e. {block_hash: KVCacheBlocks})\n    - Mostly block_hash maps to a single KVCacheBlock, and KVCacheBlocks\n        would simply be a KVCacheBlock.\n    - Otherwise, KVCacheBlocks is a dict from {block_id: KVCacheBlock}\n    用于前缀缓存（prefix caching）的块缓存。它将块哈希（hash）直接映射到单个块或多个块（即 `{block_hash: KVCacheBlocks}` 结构）\n    - 通常情况下，`block_hash` 映射到单个 `KVCacheBlock`，此时 `KVCacheBlocks` 实际上就是一个 `KVCacheBlock` 对象。 \n    - 否则，`KVCacheBlocks` 是一个 `{block_id: KVCacheBlock}` 形式的字典。\n\n    A cached block is a full block with a block hash that can be used\n    for prefix caching.\n    The cached block may be used by running requests or in the\n    free_block_queue that could potentially be evicted.\n    被缓存的块是一个完整的块，拥有可用于前缀缓存的块哈希。 \n    该缓存块可能正被正在运行的请求使用，也可能位于 `free_block_queue`（空闲块队列）中，\n    随时可能被驱逐。\n\n    NOTE #1: We currently don't de-duplicate the blocks in the cache,\n    meaning that if a block becomes full and is cached, we don't check\n    if there is already an identical block in the cache. This is because\n    we want to make sure the allocated block IDs won't change so that\n    block tables are append-only.\n    NOTE #2: The union type is introduced in order to reduce GC costs\n    from the inner dict.\n    注意 #1：目前我们不对缓存中的块进行去重处理；\n    这意味着当一个块填满并被缓存时，我们不会检查缓存中是否已存在相同的块。 \n    这样做的目的是确保已分配的块 ID 保持不变，从而保证块表（block tables）仅支持追加操作。 \n    注意 #2：引入联合类型（union type）是为了降低内部字典带来的垃圾回收（GC）开销。\n\n    \"\"\"\n\n    self._cache: dict[BlockHashWithGroupId, KVCacheBlock | dict[int, KVCacheBlock]] = {}\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 6,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "containerId": "Px3Z_Auj00x836fADOrmk",
      "originalText": "class KVCacheManager:\n\n    self.coordinator = get_kv_cache_coordinator()\n    self.block_pool = self.coordinator.block_pool\n\n\nclass KVCacheCoordinator(ABC):\n\n    self.block_pool = BlockPool()\n\n\nclass BlockPool:\n\n    # Free block queue that constructs and manipulates a doubly linked\n    # list of free blocks (including eviction candidates when caching is\n    # enabled).\n    self.free_block_queue = FreeKVCacheBlockQueue(self.blocks)\n\n    # Cache for block lookup\n    self.cached_block_hash_to_block: BlockHashToBlockMap = BlockHashToBlockMap()\n\n\nclass FreeKVCacheBlockQueue:\n    \"\"\"This class organizes a list of KVCacheBlock objects to a doubly linked\n    list of free blocks. We implement this class instead of using Python\n    builtin deque to support removing a block in the middle of the queue\n    in O(1) time. To close the performance gap to the builtin deque which is\n    implemented in C++, this class does not allocate any Python objects when\n    manipulating the linked list. Instead, this class manipulates the\n    prev_free_block and next_free_block attributes of the given blocks.\n    该类将一组 `KVCacheBlock` 对象组织成一个空闲块双向链表。\n    我们选择实现该类而非使用 Python 内置的 `deque`，是为了支持在 O(1) 时间复杂度内移除队列中间的某个块。\n    为了缩小与 C++ 实现的内置 `deque` 之间的性能差距，该类在操作链表时不会分配任何 Python 对象，\n    而是直接操作给定块的 `prev_free_block` 和 `next_free_block` 属性。\n\n    The queue is ordered by block ID in the beginning. When a block is allocated\n    and then freed, it will be appended back with the eviction order:\n    1. The least recent used block is at the front (LRU).\n    2. If two blocks have the same last accessed time (allocated by the\n       same sequence), the one with more hash tokens (the tail of a block\n       chain) is at the front.\n    Note that we maintain this order by reversing the block order when free\n    blocks of a request. This operation is outside of this class.\n    初始状态下，队列按块 ID 排序。当一个块被分配并随后释放时，它会根据以下淘汰顺序重新加入队列：\n    1. 最近最少使用（LRU）的块位于队首。\n    2. 如果两个块的最后访问时间相同（即由同一序列分配），则包含更多哈希标记（hash tokens，即块链的末端）的块位于队首。\n    请注意，我们是通过在释放请求相关的空闲块时反转块的顺序来维护这一排序的；该操作在类外部进行。\n\n    Args:\n        blocks: A list of KVCacheBlock objects.\n    \"\"\"\n\n\nclass BlockHashToBlockMap:\n    \"\"\"\n    Cache of blocks that are used for prefix caching. It caches blocks\n    from hash directly to a block or multiple blocks\n    (i.e. {block_hash: KVCacheBlocks})\n    - Mostly block_hash maps to a single KVCacheBlock, and KVCacheBlocks\n        would simply be a KVCacheBlock.\n    - Otherwise, KVCacheBlocks is a dict from {block_id: KVCacheBlock}\n    用于前缀缓存（prefix caching）的块缓存。它将块哈希（hash）直接映射到单个块或多个块（即 `{block_hash: KVCacheBlocks}` 结构）\n    - 通常情况下，`block_hash` 映射到单个 `KVCacheBlock`，此时 `KVCacheBlocks` 实际上就是一个 `KVCacheBlock` 对象。 \n    - 否则，`KVCacheBlocks` 是一个 `{block_id: KVCacheBlock}` 形式的字典。\n\n    A cached block is a full block with a block hash that can be used\n    for prefix caching.\n    The cached block may be used by running requests or in the\n    free_block_queue that could potentially be evicted.\n    被缓存的块是一个完整的块，拥有可用于前缀缓存的块哈希。 \n    该缓存块可能正被正在运行的请求使用，也可能位于 `free_block_queue`（空闲块队列）中，\n    随时可能被驱逐。\n\n    NOTE #1: We currently don't de-duplicate the blocks in the cache,\n    meaning that if a block becomes full and is cached, we don't check\n    if there is already an identical block in the cache. This is because\n    we want to make sure the allocated block IDs won't change so that\n    block tables are append-only.\n    NOTE #2: The union type is introduced in order to reduce GC costs\n    from the inner dict.\n    注意 #1：目前我们不对缓存中的块进行去重处理；\n    这意味着当一个块填满并被缓存时，我们不会检查缓存中是否已存在相同的块。 \n    这样做的目的是确保已分配的块 ID 保持不变，从而保证块表（block tables）仅支持追加操作。 \n    注意 #2：引入联合类型（union type）是为了降低内部字典带来的垃圾回收（GC）开销。\n\n    \"\"\"\n\n    self._cache: dict[BlockHashWithGroupId, KVCacheBlock | dict[int, KVCacheBlock]] = {}\n",
